      "content": "It's understandable that you're looking to find a way to address the swelling without going to the ER, but it's really important not to self-medicate with large doses of aspirin or any combination of pain relievers, as it can lead to serious health problems. Aspirin can thin your blood, which can worsen bleeding if there are any internal injuries, and when taken with ibuprofen (an NSAID), it can increase the risk of gastrointestinal bleeding and other complications. Given your symptoms, particularly the swelling in your calf and the chest tightness, it's crucial to get medical attention immediately for proper diagnosis and treatment. Do your best to see a healthcare provider, and explore options that may be available for those without insurance, such as urgent care centers or medical schools that offer low-cost services. Your health and safety are most important right now.",
